  "body": "Stacked on #1138 (on #1080, #1007). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\n**#1169 - a rapid landed on a wall strip thinner than a planner cell (safety floor).**\nThe microlift plan read its landings on the planner's cell bitmap (D/120 = 0.083 mm). A wall strip thinner than a cell that falls between two rows of cell centers is invisible there: the easing laps drop it as \"air\" and it stands until the last lap. On the narrow slot 14x60 the return over the retract plane (`LinkLaw::high`) rapided to 0.3 mm over the floor at (17.407, 8.956) with a 0.075 mm strip under its rim - the verifier's `RapidInStock`.\n\n- New `adaptive::lift_swept::Swept`: the segments the plan's pieces have cut so far, exactly. `high` lands only where the whole footprint (r - 10 um, the verifier's own footprint) is within r - 12.5 um of a cut segment (2.5 um arc fit + the 10 um chords the verifier reads a posted arc on). The proof is a quadtree over the disc on exact segment distances (1-Lipschitz bound per square, divided to 1 um); where it does not close the landing is refused. Nothing is sampled. The cell test stays as the cheap first reading. The verifier is untouched.\n- The hop's landing (`lift_link::landing`) takes a lead point the pieces swept before one only the cells read clear. The hop comes down at plunge feed from over the stock, never in rapid, so with no point proved the cells' choice stands.\n- A piece starting exactly where the tool stands is ridden on to at the floor (`lift::ride`) instead of a retract and plunge on one spot. That hop, not the strip, was the slot's \"4 descents for 2 levels\" (the growth's last piece handing over to the first easing lap at (5.135, 7.312), both in cut).\n\n**#1050 - the held fix (16e129bb), now landable.** `adaptive::conform`: the disc phase out of the entry bore is held on the planner's rim and on a rim twice as coarse (the worse kept); the closing laps' fillet kinks are spread at 4 degrees. The measured pins `R62_LOAD_FACTOR`, `R62_BREAKS` and `BAR_50_BREAKS` are removed; the pins hold the whole bar's laws. No law and no bound loosened.\n\n## Readings (release, Linux x86-64)\n\nNarrow slot 14x60, with #1050's change:\n\n| | verifier | descents (2 levels) | returns | over the retract plane | rides | hops |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| before | 1 `RapidInStock` | 4 | 200 | 3 | 0 | 1 |\n| after | silent | 2 | 199 (1365 mm lifted) | 0 | 2 | 0 |\n\nOut of cut 0.88x the cut (law 1.5), load 15.4 % D, 0 breaks, 14262 moves.\n\nRotary bars (0.1 mm dexel, law 19.8 % D, no break past 5 deg):\n\n| level | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| r6.2 / 5.7 | 20.3 % D, 0 breaks | 17.3 % D, 0 breaks |\n| r6.2 / 5.2 | 20.3 % D, 3 breaks | 17.7 % D, 0 breaks |\n| r7 / 6.5, 6.0 | - | 19.5 % D, 0 breaks |\n| r7 / 5.5, 5.0 | - | 17.3 %, 18.4 % D, 0 breaks |\n\nOther `adaptive_hsm` fixtures: bore 15.4 % D, rectangle 15.4, L-pocket 15.7, 0 breaks, 2 descents each; island and channel fall back to Offset rings as before.\n\n## Verdict moves\n\n- Narrow slot: `RapidInStock` -> silent; its three returns over the retract plane (leads along the walls, not provable at 12.5 um) became routed lifted returns; one retract hop became a ride.\n- r6.2 neck levels and r7 level 5.0: measured pins removed, now under the whole bar's laws.\n- App `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` (the STEP bore's per-platform exact triple, moves / planar feeds / arcs): the plan moved, as the pin says a planner change will. Linux x86-64 had no triple of its own (it rode the band of the other two, 16100-16260 moves); it now reads **(15561, 14837, 1561)**, two release runs identical, added as its own exact arm. Every level still verifies clean and none falls back (Z 20: 56 microlift returns, 7 rides, 1 retract hop). **The Windows (16197, 15458, 1581) and macOS (16160, 15432, 1571) triples were measured before these changes and could not be re-measured here; they are left as measured, not widened, and will fail on those platforms until re-measured there.** That re-measure is owed before this merges or at the latest at the cut (release tier).\n- No golden file and no snapshot changed.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew: `lift_swept::tests::a_rapid_landing_on_a_sub_cell_wall_strip_is_refused` (a 0.04 mm strip the cells read clear: `high` refused, allowed once the strip is cut; the hop landing's preference), `lift_swept::tests::a_disc_is_covered_on_the_cut_and_not_a_hair_past_it`, `lift_tests::a_piece_starting_where_the_tool_stands_is_ridden_on_to`.\n\nRun on the final planner code (ba3cdd8e; the commits after it change only docs and the app pin's Linux arm), release, `--include-ignored`:\n- motion `adaptive_hsm` 6/6 (`hsm_report_full_resolution` green), `adaptive_band` 2/2, `rotary_adaptive` 6/6, `level_links` 12/12, `pocket3d_hsm` 4/4, `adaptive_orbit_seam` 1/1\n- motion lib `adaptive` filter 35/35 (both #1051 budget twins, the slot sweep, the new unit tests)\n- app `shoulder_adaptive` 3/3, `roughing2d` 7/7, `pocket_overhead` 2/2, `whole_model_pocket` 5/5 (release, default lane)\n- app `pocket3d_hsm` 2/2 (with the Linux triple added; first run red on the band, see Verdict moves)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/1051-planning-budget-edge`: green (motion lib + 5 suites, debug)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The batch and release gate tiers; app suites other than `pocket3d_hsm`; the UI.\n- Windows and macOS: nothing was run there, and the bore pin's triples for both are stale (Verdict moves).\n- Which of the two changes moved the bore's triple was not separated (the held #1050 commit was never run against that suite on its own).\n- The hop landing's swept preference on a real plan: no fixture run here posts a hop after this change (unit-tested only).\n- The ramp down a lead is still read on the cells: it is a feed above the floor, so a sub-cell strip under it is cut, not collided with (decision file).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1169-landing-on-swept-stock.md`, `docs/decisions/1050-developed-band-exit.md`.\n\nChangelog: Adaptive: a return over the retract plane lands only where the cut pieces provably swept the whole tool footprint (no rapid onto a wall strip thinner than a planner cell); abutting pieces ride on instead of a retract and plunge; the bore exit on a developed band holds the load law on coarse measuring grids and the closing laps post no break past 5 degrees (#1169, #1050)\n\nEffort: max (#1050 escalated from high)\n\nFixes #1169\nFixes #1050\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
